Z||000002||ray b||02-02-2001||06:19 PM||||take off rear eng coolant cap, and run car to see if it bubbles in coolant if it does you got bad head gasket or cracked head look for leaks if no bubbles. ray||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||02-02-2001||11:30 PM||||ok, got myself a new 16lb cap and it seems to be doing ok. of course it always does ok for a while, then screws up again. i did what you said ray. i filled it up in the back till i could see it, let it run a bit and i noticed some air bubbles. i think it was just working air out of the system. after a little while, i didn't notice any more air bubbles and turned it off. then i topped it off, put in the stat, and put the cap back on. drove it around a few miles and it did ok.<BR>i don't notice any leaks anywhere. and i did a compression test a while back and it checked out ok. not real good, but not too bad. i'm thinking about checking that again sometime.<BR>i was told different things about the excessive smoke. could be the valve seals or the rings. i don't know enough about cars to determine anything about this.||||reg||1
